<title>EGYPT: Egypt pound overnight rates rise in short market.</title>
<headline>Egypt pound overnight rates rise in short market.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1996-12-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Overnight interbank rates on the Egyptian pound rose on Sunday to between 10.25 and 10.375 percent in a slightly short market from Thursday's range of 9.75 and 10.25 percent, bankers said.</p>
<p>One-week rates were unchanged from Thursday's range of 10.125 to 10.25.</p>
<p>State-owned banks maintained their minimum overnight lending rate at 10.5 percent, bankers said.</p>
<p>-- Cairo newsroom +20 2 578 3290/1</p>
